Rule ID:	xccdf_mil.disa.stig_rule_SV-271427r1137691_rule
Test Type:	Automated
Rule Applicability:	Windows_DomainController
Rule Result:	Not Applicable
Version:	WN22-DC-000406
Identities:	CCI-000213 (NIST SP 800-53: AC-3; NIST SP 800-53A: AC-3.1; NIST SP 800-53 Rev 4: AC-3; NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5: AC-3)
Description:	Weak mappings give rise to security vulnerabilities and demand hardening measures. Certificate names must be correctly mapped to the intended user account in Active Directory. A lack of strong name-based mappings allows certain weak certificate mappings, such as Issuer/Subject AltSecID and User Principal Names (UPN) mappings, to be treated as strong mappings.
Check Text:	This applies to domain controllers. This is not applicable for member servers.

Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.

Run "gpedit.msc".

Navigate to Local Computer Policy >> Computer Configuration >> Administrative Template >> System >> KDC >> Allow name-based strong mappings for certificates.

If "Allow name-based strong mappings for certificates" is not "Enabled", this is a finding.
Fix Text:	Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Administrative Template >> System >> KDC >> Allow name-based strong mappings for certificates to "Enabled".
